At 1200 visibilities (4.2 data points per mesh pixel) `--criterion auto`
takes `discrepancy`, and the demo delivered a residual map at 0.51 sigma.
This was documented as a small-mock artefact (the map not being white);
it is not: pure noise through the same imager reads 0.95-1.02 over five
realisations, so the model absorbed noise. With a truth the 24x24 mesh
cannot fully represent, chi^2 = N is reached by fitting noise, while
`structure` at that size leaves signal instead (chi^2/N 1.30).

At 4800 visibilities auto takes `structure` and the residual map is white
(1.06 against 1.05 expected; the point recovered at 3.98 mJy of 4.0).
`pyuvimage demo` now uses 4800; the generator's default is unchanged for
the tests. The run takes about 2 min in the container instead of seconds.

